ARTSynchronized (flode, master f00003e), OptimisticLockCoupling/Tree.cpp and Tree.h: the compressed-prefix
seek of the START-ONLY Tree::lookupRange(start, result[], resultLen, resultCount, ti). Its main loop
(the descent from the root, which continues only along a start byte 0xff) handled a node whose
compressed prefix compares BIGGER than start -- start diverges inside the prefix with a smaller byte, so
every key below the node is greater than start -- exactly like an EQUAL one: it selected the node's
children by the start byte at the mismatch position (checkPrefixCompare stops there) instead of the byte
after the prefix, so children labelled below that byte were skipped although all their keys are >= start
(stored {ff 'c' 'a', ff 'c' 'z'}, start ff 'b': only ff 'c' 'z' was returned). The recursive findStart
already copies a Bigger subtree whole; the patch makes the main loop do the same. Reachable only below the
root's 0xff child: the root (an N256) never carries a prefix. Tree.h gains the marker
ART_OLC_TRIE_BENCH_SCAN_FIXES, which the benchmark adapter requires before it exposes the scan. Apply on
top of artsync_olc_prefix_race.patch and artsync_olc_scan_null_child.patch (campaign copy
~/dictcmp/baselines/ARTSynchronized; trie/bench/adapters/artsync_adapter.hpp documents all three and the
adapter's own leading-key filter). Insert and lookup code is unchanged.
